              <div class="kdm-topic-content">
                <h4>Social Media Marketing</h4>
                <p>platform-specific strategy, organic growth tactics, influencer collaboration, and paid social. A
                  well-researched social media marketing guest post with real campaign examples performs especially well
                  with our audience.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="kdm-topic-card">
              <div class="kdm-topic-icon"><i class="fa fa-cogs"></i></div>
              <div class="kdm-topic-content">
                <h4>Marketing Technology & Automation</h4>
                <p>CRM integrations, email automation, AI tools for marketers, analytics platforms, and martech stack
                  reviews. Because this space evolves quickly, our technology guest post guidelines and broader guest
                  post guidelines technology standards require that every tool or platform claim be current and
                  verifiable.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="kdm-topic-card">
              <div class="kdm-topic-icon"><i class="fa fa-pie-chart"></i></div>
              <div class="kdm-topic-content">
                <h4>Paid Media and PPC</h4>
                <p>Google Ads, paid social, programmatic advertising, and campaign optimization case studies.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="kdm-topic-card">
              <div class="kdm-topic-icon"><i class="fa fa-briefcase"></i></div>
              <div class="kdm-topic-content">
                <h4>Branding and Business Growth</h4>
                <p>positioning, customer acquisition, conversion rate optimization, and marketing leadership.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="kdm-topic-card" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
              <div class="kdm-topic-icon"><i class="fa fa-calculator"></i></div>
              <div class="kdm-topic-content">
                <h4>Finance and Marketing Crossover</h4>
                <p>marketing budgeting, ROI attribution, and growth finance topics. Writers coming from a finance
                  background should treat our finance guest post guidelines the same way as any other category:
                  practical, data-backed, and free of generic filler.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-callout">
            If your topic idea doesn't fit neatly into one of these buckets but is still relevant to digital marketing
            professionals, pitch us anyway. We evaluate every guest post submission individually rather than rejecting
            on category alone.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3: Our Content Standards -->
        <div class="kdm-card">
          <h2 class="kdm-section-title"><i class="fa fa-shield"></i> Our Content Standards</h2>
          <p class="kdm-lead-text">
            We built these guest posting guidelines to protect the quality of our publication and to make sure every
            reader who lands on an article gets real value. Before you draft anything, keep the following in mind:
          </p>

          <div class="kdm-standard-item">
            <div class="kdm-standard-num">1</div>
            <div class="kdm-standard-body">
              <h4>Original, Unpublished Content Only</h4>
              <p>Every article submitted through our digital marketing submit guest post process must be 100% original
                and never published anywhere else &mdash; not on your own blog, not on Medium, not on another guest
                posting site. We run originality checks on all submissions, and duplicate or AI-spun content is an
                automatic rejection.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-standard-item">
            <div class="kdm-standard-num">2</div>
            <div class="kdm-standard-body">
              <h4>Minimum Word Count</h4>
              <p>Articles should run at least 1,200&ndash;1,800 words. Short posts rarely offer enough depth to rank or
                to genuinely help the reader, so when you submit a guest post digital marketing audiences will actually
                use, aim for thorough coverage rather than padding a shorter draft to hit a number.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-standard-item">
            <div class="kdm-standard-num">3</div>
            <div class="kdm-standard-body">
              <h4>Real Expertise, Not Generic Advice</h4>
              <p>The single biggest reason we decline a submit guest post digital marketing pitch is that it reads like
                a repackaged listicle everyone has already seen. We want first-hand experience: campaign results, tools
                you've actually tested, mistakes you've made and fixed, and specific numbers wherever possible.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-standard-item">
            <div class="kdm-standard-num">4</div>
            <div class="kdm-standard-body">
              <h4>Structure That's Easy to Scan</h4>
              <p>Use clear H2 and H3 subheadings, short paragraphs, and bullet points where appropriate. Most readers
                scan before they commit to reading in full, so a logical structure with descriptive headings increases
                both engagement time and shareability.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-standard-item">
            <div class="kdm-standard-num">5</div>
            <div class="kdm-standard-body">
              <h4>Linking Policy</h4>
              <p>We allow one contextual link back to your own site within the body of the article (non-promotional,
                genuinely useful to the reader) plus one link in your author bio. Excessive linking, affiliate links, or
                links to unrelated commercial pages will result in edits or rejection. This applies whether you're
                contributing a guest post + digital marketing piece or a niche technical article.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-standard-item">
            <div class="kdm-standard-num">6</div>
            <div class="kdm-standard-body">
              <h4>No Plagiarism or Spun Content</h4>
              <p>This is non-negotiable across every category, from a guest blog post guidelines submission on content
                strategy to a technical SEO deep-dive. We check every submission before publishing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-standard-item">
            <div class="kdm-standard-num">7</div>
            <div class="kdm-standard-body">
              <h4>Images and Formatting</h4>
              <p>Include at least one original or properly licensed image, chart, or screenshot to support your points.
                Avoid stock photography that doesn't add real context.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4: How to Submit a Guest Post -->
        <div class="kdm-card">
          <h2 class="kdm-section-title"><i class="fa fa-paper-plane"></i> How to Submit a Guest Post</h2>
          <p class="kdm-lead-text">
            Here's the exact process we ask every contributor to follow when they submit blog post ideas or full drafts
            to King of Digital Marketing:
          </p>

          <div class="kdm-step-item">
            <div class="kdm-step-badge">1</div>
            <div class="kdm-step-content">
              <h4>Pitch your idea first</h4>
              <p>Rather than sending a completed article cold, send us a short pitch: your proposed headline, a
                two-to-three sentence outline of what the article will cover, and a note on your relevant experience.
                This saves you time if the topic overlaps with something we've recently published.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-step-item">
            <div class="kdm-step-badge">2</div>
            <div class="kdm-step-content">
              <h4>Wait for approval</h4>
              <p>Our editorial team typically responds within 2&ndash;4 business days. If your topic fits our current
                content calendar and hasn't been covered recently, we'll green-light it and give you any specific notes.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-step-item">
            <div class="kdm-step-badge">3</div>
            <div class="kdm-step-content">
              <h4>Write and submit the full draft</h4>
              <p>Once approved, write the complete article following the standards above. Submit it as a Google Doc link
                or plain text file, along with:</p>
              <ul class="kdm-step-list">
                <li>A 2&ndash;3 sentence author bio</li>
                <li>Your headshot (optional but recommended)</li>
                <li>Your preferred backlink and anchor text</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-step-item">
            <div class="kdm-step-badge">4</div>
            <div class="kdm-step-content">
              <h4>Editorial review</h4>
              <p>We review every guest post marketing submission for originality, accuracy, structure, and alignment
                with our audience. We may request revisions before publishing &mdash; this is normal and doesn't mean
                rejection.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-step-item">
            <div class="kdm-step-badge">5</div>
            <div class="kdm-step-content">
              <h4>Publication</h4>
              <p>Once approved, we schedule the article for publication and notify you with the live link. Please allow
                a reasonable window for edits, formatting, and internal linking on our end before the piece goes live.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-callout">
            This is essentially our full guest posting guide in five steps &mdash; simple, transparent, and designed to
            respect both your time and our readers' trust.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5: Dual Card Section - Don't Accept & Pitch Tips -->
        <div class="kdm-grid-2">
          <div class="kdm-alert-reject">
            <h4><i class="fa fa-times-circle"></i> What We Don't Accept</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #742a2a; margin-bottom: 12px;">To keep our marketing guest post guidelines
              consistent and fair to everyone, we do not accept:</p>
            <ul class="kdm-list-styled reject">
              <li>Content that has been published elsewhere, in whole or in part</li>
              <li>Articles stuffed with keywords rather than written for readers</li>
              <li>Thin content under our minimum word count</li>
              <li>Unrelated topics outside digital marketing, SEO, content, social, martech, or business growth</li>
              <li>Guest posts written primarily to promote a product, with the "advice" as an afterthought</li>
              <li>Content generated entirely by AI without meaningful human research, editing, and expertise</li>
              <li>Multiple link requests, paid link placements, or link schemes that violate search engine guidelines
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p style="font-size: 13px; color: #9b2c2c; margin-top: 14px; font-style: italic;">
              If you're unsure whether your idea fits, send a quick pitch before writing the full piece &mdash; it's a
              lot faster than reworking a finished draft.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-alert-tips">
            <h4><i class="fa fa-lightbulb-o"></i> Tips for a Stronger Pitch</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #14532d; margin-bottom: 12px;">Whether this is your first time trying to
              submit guest post content anywhere or you've contributed to dozens of publications, these tips will
              improve your odds with us specifically:</p>
            <ul class="kdm-list-styled tips">
              <li><strong>Study a few of our existing articles first.</strong> Match our tone: practical, direct, and
                free of fluff.</li>
              <li><strong>Bring a unique angle.</strong> If you're pitching something broad like "SEO tips for 2026,"
                narrow it down to something specific &mdash; a strategy you've personally tested, a niche vertical, or a
                data-backed contrarian take.</li>
              <li><strong>Use real examples.</strong> Case studies, screenshots of results, or even anonymized client
                data make an article far more credible than generic advice.</li>
              <li><strong>Keep the pitch short.</strong> Editors are busy; a tight, well-organized pitch gets read
                faster than a long one.</li>
              <li><strong>Be patient but responsive.</strong> If we request revisions, quick turnaround on your end
                keeps the process moving and improves your chances for future contributions.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="font-size: 13px; color: #166534; margin-top: 14px; font-style: italic;">
              We genuinely value contributors who treat guest posting in digital marketing as a long-term relationship
              rather than a single transaction. Writers who consistently deliver high-quality, original work are welcome
              to contribute regularly and may be considered for a dedicated author profile on our site.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6: Ready to Contribute CTA Card -->
        <div class="kdm-cta-card">
          <h4>Ready to Contribute?</h3>
          <p>
            If you've read through our guest post guidelines and you're ready to move forward, send us your pitch with a
            proposed topic, a short outline, and a line or two about your background in digital marketing, SEO, content,
            social media, or martech. We look forward to reviewing your idea and, if it's a fit, publishing your work to
            an audience of engaged marketing professionals.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 7: Frequently Asked Questions -->
        <div class="kdm-card">
          <h2 class="kdm-section-title"><i class="fa fa-question-circle"></i> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="kdm-faq-item">
            <div class="kdm-faq-question">
              <span>1. What topics can I write about for a digital marketing guest post?</span>
              <i class="fa fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="kdm-faq-answer">
              We accept articles on SEO, content marketing, social media marketing, marketing technology, PPC and paid
              media, branding, business growth, and the finance side of marketing. If your topic idea falls within
              digital marketing broadly and offers genuine, practical value, it's worth pitching even if it doesn't fit
              neatly into one category.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-faq-item">
            <div class="kdm-faq-question">
              <span>2. Is King of Digital Marketing currently accepting guest posts?</span>
              <i class="fa fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="kdm-faq-answer">
              Yes. We are actively accepting guest posts from experienced marketers, agency professionals, and
              subject-matter experts. We review pitches on a rolling basis, so there's no fixed submission window
              &mdash; you can send your idea at any time.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-faq-item">
            <div class="kdm-faq-question">
              <span>3. How do I submit a guest post to your site?</span>
              <i class="fa fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="kdm-faq-answer">
              Start by sending a short pitch that includes your proposed headline, a brief outline, and a note on your
              relevant experience. Once approved, you'll write the full draft following our content standards and submit
              it along with your author bio and preferred backlink. Full details are outlined in the submission process
              above.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-faq-item">
            <div class="kdm-faq-question">
              <span>4. Do you allow backlinks in guest posts, and are there restrictions?</span>
              <i class="fa fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="kdm-faq-answer">
              Yes, we allow one relevant, contextual link within the article body and one link in your author bio. We
              don't allow excessive linking, affiliate links, or links unrelated to the article's topic. Any link scheme
              or paid placement request will result in rejection.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kdm-faq-item">
            <div class="kdm-faq-question">
              <span>5. How long does it take to get a guest post approved and published?</span>
              <i class="fa fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="kdm-faq-answer">
              Pitch reviews typically take 2&ndash;4 business days. After you submit the full draft, editorial review
              can take another few days depending on how much revision is needed. Once approved, we schedule publication
              and send you the live link as soon as it's up.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

